WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.670
Filling in your project kit, the draft steps.

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.010
This is the kit for Cragmoor,

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.530
a made-up chain of climbing gyms.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.730
Your company's kit has the same rows in the same places.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.530
The grey cells are numbers from

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:17.850
the company's reports filled in for you.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:20.190
The yellow cells are yours.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.490
Next to every yellow cell,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.650
column C tells you which cells to use.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.650
Step one, builds one full year of cash flow for

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.350
one new gym. The first yellow cell is the cash profit before tax.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.310
Column C says revenue times cash margin,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.890
so I'll type equals B times B50 and press Enter.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.310
That's 1.7 million.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.030
I'll fill in the next four rows the same way,

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:49.870
reading column C each time.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.730
A full year's cash flow comes to about 1.21 million.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.350
The last cell is year zero,

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.190
the cost to open the gym.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.070
That's money going out,

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:02.870
so I'll type it as a negative number.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.290
Under every step, there's a check row.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.250
When every cell is right,

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.370
it shows a check mark.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.870
If a cell is wrong,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.690
it tells you which one to fix.

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:13.550
Step two is the hurdle rate,

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:16.910
worked in dollars, the same way as the food trucks.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:21.330
The owner's stake is the number of shares times today's share price.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.670
The return the owners expect is the treasury rate

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:27.430
plus beta times the market premium.

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.130
Then come the dollars a year for lenders,

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.390
the dollars a year for owners,

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:34.730
and the hurdle rate,

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:38.690
which is the total dollars divided by all the money put in.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.210
For Cragmoor, that's 9.4%.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.010
In step three, the year table fills itself in

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.190
from your step one and step two cells.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:51.570
Each year's cash flow is brought back to today

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:53.190
at your hurdle rate.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:59.410
You type one formula equals sum of the present value column.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.410
Cragmoor's NPV is 1.91 million.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:04.910
It's above zero.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.470
So on these numbers, one new gym is worth building.

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.230
Step four asks how wrong these numbers could be.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.210
The base case is filled in for you.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.670
You choose a worst case and a best case for each input.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.050
And each choice should come from something in your fact sheet.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.910
Cragmoor's newer gyms earned between 4.3 million

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.070
and 5.6 million a year.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:29.910
So I'll use those for revenue.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.290
As I type, the kit works out the NPV of each case.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.950
In my worst case, the gym loses 2.15 million.

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:41.850
In my best case, it adds 5.47 million.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.550
That range is what your draft memo is about.

00:02:46.120 --> 00:02:48.470
The NPV, your worst and best cases,

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.510
and what would have to be true for your answer to change.
